commit afb18cccd9da322700048f40467a1c6780123f8e
Author: Thomas Klemm <github@tklemm.eu>
Date:   Fri Nov 27 16:14:03 2026 +0000

    Append backtrace location strings by length
    
    Formatting a backtrace location through "%"PRIsVALUE runs each file
    and method name through rb_obj_as_string, an encoding check and
    StringValueCStr in ruby__sfvextra. That makes Exception#backtrace and
    Kernel#caller about 25% slower than 4.0 on a 150-frame stack, and
    StringValueCStr raises ArgumentError for a path that contains a NUL
    byte, so the backtrace of code evaluated with such a path cannot be
    built at all.
    
    Append both strings by their length instead, choosing the encoding
    the same way ruby__sfvextra does.

diff --git a/benchmark/vm_backtrace_to_s.yml b/benchmark/vm_backtrace_to_s.yml
